+### Source file approval in PR #32
+
+The source-delivery implementation in [PR #32](https://github.com/mksdr/Miroven/pull/32) uses `web/scripts/source-files.json` to approve individual distribution input paths. `npm run sources:check` runs before Next.js; packaging checks again. Unlisted files inside the source roots, missing approved files, forbidden names and symlinks fail the build. Private/generated roots stay excluded. This describes the PR implementation, not an already verified production deployment.
+
+When adding, removing or renaming source files, stage only intended public paths with `git add -- <paths>`, run `npm run sources:update` from `web/`, and review the file-list diff. The update command derives candidates from tracked paths; untracked and ignored files are not auto-approved. Move private files outside source roots instead of approving them to pass a build. Ordinary builds never regenerate the list.
+
+The list travels with the source archive, so Docker contexts and extracted-source builds work without Git metadata. Approved files keep their actual local modifications; approval concerns paths and does not certify that their contents contain no secrets. Adding files to a downloaded source tree requires explicitly reviewing/editing its list or using a Git checkout and the update command. See [the bilingual source approval workflow](https://github.com/mksdr/Miroven/blob/fix/heic-lgpl-source-delivery/tools/heic/README.md).
